# Session and video UI legibility

Sessions are recorded in **presenter mode** and published on **YouTube** (1080p). Every **user-visible** label, body line, code bubble, and control in session components, gallery demos, and MDX interactives must read **at a glance** on stream — not only on a laptop at arm’s length.

**Default assumption:** you are designing a **slide**, not a dense app UI.

## Typography (must-follow)

### Minimum sizes (never go below for teaching content)

| Role | Tailwind minimum | Notes |
|------|------------------|--------|
| In-component headings (`h2`/`h3`) | `text-xl md:text-2xl` | Prefer `text-2xl md:text-3xl` on full-slide panels |
| Body / explanations / step detail | `text-lg md:text-xl` | Prefer `text-xl md:text-2xl` when the panel is the only visual on the slide |
| Section labels (e.g. “USER INPUT”, “TOKENS”) | `text-base md:text-lg` | `font-bold`, letter-spacing; **never** `text-xs` |
| API / JSON / monospace payloads | `text-base md:text-lg` | Prefer `text-lg md:text-xl` in hero code bubbles |
| Buttons / toggles / step controls | `text-base md:text-lg` | Large tap targets: `py-3 px-5` minimum |
| Secondary hints only | `text-base` | Do not put the **only** explanation of a concept at hint size |

### Banned for essential copy

- `text-xs`, `text-sm` (as primary teaching text), `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]`
- Faint critical labels: `text-gray-500` on dark shells for anything the presenter must read aloud

### When in doubt

Bump **one step larger** rather than fitting more on screen. Fewer words per panel is better than smaller type.

## Blocks, spacing, and contrast

- **Outer panels:** `p-8 md:p-10` for full-slide interactives; `space-y-6`–`space-y-10` between major blocks
- **Inner cards:** `p-5 md:p-6` minimum
- **Chips / pills:** `py-3 px-4` minimum; hero rows (tokens, params) `text-lg md:text-2xl` with `ring-1` or border for separation on video
- **Contrast (dark shells):** body `text-gray-100`–`text-gray-200`; secondary `text-gray-300`–`text-gray-400` only

## SVG and diagrams

- Label text in SVGs: roughly **16px+** in user units (`text-sm` equivalent or larger); avoid 9–10px axis labels except rare ticks
- Match `.cursor/rules/ppt-title-diagram-only.mdc` and `docs/session-template.md` § Diagram clarity

## New and edited components

Any **new** session-facing component must meet this rule in the **first PR**. When touching existing components for a session, **upgrade typography in that component** rather than adding another tiny pattern.

Non-user-facing code (`lib/`, types, tests) is exempt — but do not export new tiny UI from shared session barrels.
